-- title:
--   Ld Sandwich Line One Point Endpoint Comm Error Le
-- statement:
--   **The endpoint commutation terms fit inside the line one-point error envelope.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `eps`, `delta`, `gamma`, and `zeta` be nonnegative errors with $\zeta\le1$, and let natural numbers `j` and `k` satisfy $1\le j\le k$. Then the sum of the self-consistency term, the axis/self-consistency transport square root, and twice the length-`j` half-sandwich square root is bounded by the displayed line one-point error at length `k`:
--
--   $$
--   \zeta+\sqrt{8m\min(\varepsilon,1)+4\min(\delta,1)}
--    +2\sqrt{\operatorname{commuteGHalfSandwichError}(\mathrm{params},\gamma,\zeta,j)}
--   \le\operatorname{ldSandwichLineOnePointError}(\mathrm{params},\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta,k).
--   $$
--
--   Here $m$ is the dimension parameter in `params`. Monotonicity in the chain length and the explicit power-law error envelope absorb the shorter endpoint terms into the length-`k` bound used by the line consistency theorem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.ldSandwichLineOnePoint_endpoint_comm_error_le`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
